In doubly linked list, each node contains a value and two links pointing to the previous and next node respectively. We will implement a function to insert at the end of the doubly linked list.

Here is a simple Python implementation of a node class that we will be using:

```python
class Node:
    def __init__(self, data=None):
        self.data = data
        self.next = None
        self.prev = None
```

Create doubly linked list:

```python
class DoublyLinkedList:
    def __init__(self):
        self.head = None
        self.tail = None

    def insert(self, data):
        if data is None:
            return
        else:
            if self.head is None:
                self.head = Node(data)
                self.tail = self.head
            else:
                curr = self.head
                while(curr.next != None):
                    if curr.data == data:  # Handling Duplicate values
                        return 
                    curr = curr.next
                if curr.data == data:
                    return
                new_node = Node(data)
                curr.next = new_node
                new_node.prev = curr
                self.tail = new_node
```

The code above has `O(n)` complexity because it has to go through all the elements of the linked list to check if the element already exists. But you asked for insertion operation with `O(1)` time complexity, then we have to compromise on checking for duplicates, because it costs `O(n)` time. Here is the code with `O(1)` complexity for insertion operation:

```python
class DoublyLinkedList:
    def __init__(self):
        self.head = None
        self.tail = None

    def insert(self, data):
        if data is None:
            return
        else:
            new_node = Node(data)
            if self.head is None:
                self.head = self.tail = new_node
            else:
                new_node.prev = self.tail
                self.tail.next = new_node
                self.tail = new_node
```

This implementation inserts nodes at the end of the linked list, and no duplicate checking is performed to ensure O(1) time complexity.

