Here's how you can create a function to rotate three parameters in a circular manner in Java using an array. The function will take three parameters and the first will be moved to the second, the second to the third and the third back to the first in a circular rotation.

```Java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int a = 1, b = 2, c = 3;
        System.out.println("Before rotation: a=" + a + ", b=" + b + ", c=" + c);
        rotate(a, b, c);
    }

    static void rotate(int a, int b, int c) {
        int[] arr = {a, b, c};
        int temp = arr[0];
        arr[0] = arr[1];
        arr[1] = arr[2];
        arr[2] = temp;
        System.out.println("After rotation: a=" + arr[0] + ", b=" + arr[1] + ", c=" + arr[2]);
    }
}
