This code consists of two main parts: `Map` function and `Reduce` function 

Finally, there is the `Driver` class to perform tasks like data loading, setting Mapreduce classes, data output and error handling.

The `Map` Function:

```java
static class MapTask extends Mapper<LongWritable, Text, Text, IntWritable> {

    protected void map(LongWritable keyIn, Text valueIn, Context context)
            throws IOException, InterruptedException {

        String line = valueIn.toString();
        String[] fields = line.split(","); // Assuming data is comma-separated

        String desiredKey = fields[0]; // Assuming the key of interest is in the first position
        int desiredValue = Integer.parseInt(fields[1]); // Assuming the corresponding value is in the second position

        context.write(new Text(desiredKey), new IntWritable(desiredValue));
    }
}
```

The `Reduce` function:

```java
static class ReduceTask extends Reducer<Text, IntWritable, Text, IntWritable> {

    protected void reduce(Text keyIn, Iterable<IntWritable> valuesIn, Context context)
            throws IOException, InterruptedException {

        int sum = 0;
        for (IntWritable value : valuesIn) {
            sum += value.get();
        }

        context.write(keyIn, new IntWritable(sum));
    }
}
```

