```

3. Create a new file:
Create a new JavaScript file named "server.js":

```shell
touch server.js
```
4. Write the server code:
Write a simple server using the 'http' module. This code creates a server and listens on port 3000. Every time a connected user sends a request, the server will send a response with "Hello, World!".

```js
const http = require('http');

http.createServer((req, res) => {
    res.writeHead(200, {'Content-Type': 'text/plain'});
    res.end('Hello, World!\n');
}).listen(3000);

console.log('Server running at http://localhost:3000/');
```

5. Run the server:
You can run the server using the below command:

```shell
node server.js
```

6. Open and test using a web browser:
