    charPos = charArray[position];
    System.out.println(charPos);
} else {
    System.out.println("Invalid position, string not long enough.");
}
```
This can help prevent any ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsExceptions from occurring. For a string of special characters or any other string, unless it's empty, the program should perform the same without any issues. The only thing it is doing is accessing specific index positions, which should work the same regardless of what the actual characters are. The only edge case not currently properly addressed is the empty strings which have been addressed by checking the length of the string beforehand.

