Here is a JavaScript function for removing duplicates from an array using the concept of Set:

```javascript
function removeDuplicates(array) {
  return [...new Set(array)];
}
```
The Set object lets you store unique values of any type, whether primitive values or object references. When an Array is passed to a Set, it automatically removes the duplicate values. Then we can destructure it back into an Array. 

If you want a plain JavaScript function without using Set:

```javascript
function removeDuplicates(array) {
  let uniqueArray = [];

  for(let i of array) {
    if(uniqueArray.indexOf(i) === -1) {
      uniqueArray.push(i);
    }
  }

  return uniqueArray;
}
```
The second function above uses an array to store unique values and indexOf function to check if a value is already present in uniqueArray. If not present, it will add the value to uniqueArray.

