In Java, you can easily iterate over a 2D array using nested for loops. Below is the Java method which uses the double for loops to iterate over the all elements of the 2D array and compute their aggregate:

```java
public static int aggregateOfArray(int[][] arr) {
    int aggregate = 0;
    // Nested loops to go through each element
    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < arr[i].length; j++) {
            aggregate += arr[i][j];
        }
    }
    return aggregate;
}

public static void main(String[] args) {
    int arr[][]={{1,2,3},{4,5,6}};
    System.out.println(aggregateOfArray(arr));
}
