In the code above, 'arraySearch()' function iterates over the array and checks if the current element in iteration is equal to the provided integer. If a match is found, it returns the index of the element, else it continues to the next element. If the function iterates over the entire array and no match is found, it returns -1.

二分搜索演算法是一種效率很高的搜索演算法。基礎的想法是每次在序列中都測試中間的項目。如果這個項目超出搜索範圍，就在序列的左半段或右半段重複那個過程。在 C++ 中，你可以用如下的方式來實現：

```cpp
#include <iostream>

int binarySearch(int arr[], int start, int end, int x){
    if(end >= start){
        int mid = start + (end - start)/2;      //Find the middle of the array

        if(arr[mid] == x)    //If middle is the required element,
            return mid;

        // If x greater, ignore left half
        if(arr[mid] < x)
            return binarySearch(arr, mid + 1, end, x);

        // If x is smaller, ignore right half
        return binarySearch(arr, start, mid - 1, x);
    }

    // Returns -1 if the element is not present in the array.
    return -1; 
}

int main(){
    int arr[] = {2, 3, 4, 10, 40};
    int size = sizeof(arr)/ sizeof(arr[0]);
    int find = 10;
    int result = binarySearch(arr, 0, size - 1, find);
    (result == -1) ? printf("Element is not present in array")
               : printf("Element is present at index %d", result);
    return 0;
}
```

在上述程式碼中，二進制搜尋函數需要一個排序過的數組和需要搜尋的值。如果位於中間的元素是需要搜尋的值，那麼函數就會返回。如果需要搜尋的元素比中間的元素大，那麼函數就會在數組的右半部分進行搜尋。如果需要搜尋的元素比中間的元素小，那麼函數就會在數組的左半部分進行搜尋。

在最壞的情況下，二分搜索的時間複雜度是 O(log n)，空間複雜度是 O(1)。

進一步優化的可能性主要在於改進分割策略，例如使用插值或斐波那契搜尋等方式。不過，請注意這樣的優化通常僅在特定的情況下有效，尤其是對數據分佈有特殊要求的情況。對於一般的應用場景，簡單的二分搜索已經足夠高效。

Java provides a built-in Queue interface that you can use to create queue data structures. It offers several methods like add(), poll(), peek(), etc to perform different operations on a queue.

Unfortunately, once items are added to the queue, there's no simple way to amend or change those items, because of the nature of the FIFO structure. However, if you know the exact position of the item in the queue that needs to be amended, you could create a new method in a custom class that handles a queue, and recreate the queue with the amendment.

Here is how you can create such a method:

```java
import java.util.LinkedList;
import java.util.Queue;

public class AmendableQueue {
    private Queue<String> queue;

    public AmendableQueue(Queue<String> queue) {
        this.queue = queue;
    }

    public void printQueue() {
        for (String item : queue) {
            System.out.print(item + " ");
        }
        System.out.println();
    }

    public void amendQueue(int position, String newItem) {
        Queue<String> newQueue = new LinkedList<>();
        int i = 0;

        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {
            String item = queue.poll();

            if (i == position) {
                newQueue.add(newItem);
            } else {
                newQueue.add(item);
            }

            i++;
        }

        this.queue = newQueue;
    }
}

```

This class creates an "AmendableQueue" object that takes an object of type "Queue<String>" as its main data structure. The amendQueue() method retrieves and then removes elements from the original queue and re-inserts them into a new queue. If it gets to the position that needs to be amended, it inserts the new item instead of the old one.

Please note that queue positions start from 0, so if you want to amend the first item in the queue (the first item that will get dequeued), you would pass 0 as the position.

