```
Please note you will need to run this JavaScript function in an environment where the tables exist in the Document Object Model (DOM). One option is to include it in a script tag on a webpage that contains the tables. Then call `tableToJson('tableId')` where 'tableId' is the id of the table you want to convert into JSON.

Also note that this function strictly assumes that the first row of each table contains the headers (th elements). The rest of the rows are assumed to contain the data (td elements). If your HTML tables are not structured this way, you will need to modify this function to suit your needs.

