In this code, we define the Employee class with three instance variables: employeeID, name, and tenure. The pension is calculated based on tenure: for each year of tenure less than 5 years, the employee gets 1000 units of pension, and for each year of tenure 5 years or more, the employee gets 2000 units of pension. If a non-numeric tenure is entered, the calculate_pension method will return an error message.

Moreover, employee.validate() method is implemented to handle common errors such as entering invalid data types for employeeID, name or tenure. It checks whether the data types of these inputs are correct and returns a corresponding message.

