In the above code, the replaceAndAlternate function goes through each character of the string and checks if it is a non-alphabetical or non-numeric character using a Regex test. If the condition is met, the function replaces the character with '#'. If not, it checks whether the index of the character is even or odd using the modulus operator. If the index is even, the character is converted to uppercase. If the index is odd, the character is converted to lowercase. 

Finally, the function returns the updated string.

