```java
import java.util.LinkedHashSet;

public class NonRepeatedAlphabet {

    public static String removeRepeats(String input) {
        LinkedHashSet<Character> charSet = new LinkedHashSet<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < input.length(); i++) {
            charSet.add(input.charAt(i));
        }

        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (Character character : charSet) {
            sb.append(character);
        }

        return sb.toString();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(removeRepeats("aaaBBBBcccDDD__"));
        System.out.println(removeRepeats("1111222333"));
    }
}
```

We use a `LinkedHashSet` to ensure that insertion order is preserved while duplicates are removed.
After assembling the set of characters, we build a `String` out of it.

