Here is a simple method in Java that counts the number of special characters in a string. It uses a regular expression to match non-alphanumeric characters, then counts the number of matches.

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String testStr = "Hello, World! @java #programming $test";
        System.out.println(countSpecialCharacters(testStr));
    }

    public static int countSpecialCharacters(String s) {
        int specialCharCount = 0;
        for(int i=0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            if(!Character.isLetterOrDigit(s.charAt(i))) {
                specialCharCount++;
            }
        }
        return specialCharCount;
    }
}
