```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main() {
    // Define the character arrays
    char x[] = "Hello";
    char y[] = "World!";

    // Get the lengths of the arrays
    int length_x = strlen(x);
    int length_y = strlen(y);

    // Print the array with the superior length
    if(length_x > length_y) {
        printf("The array with the superior length is x: %s\n", x);
    } else if(length_y > length_x) {
        printf("The array with the superior length is y: %s\n", y);
    } else {
        printf("Both arrays have the same length.\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
```
Here, the `strlen` function is used to get the length of the arrays which includes the null character at the end. The lengths are then compared, and the array with the superior length is printed. If the lengths are equal, a corresponding message is printed.

