Here's a basic example of a react component for displaying a rating out of five stars. It assumes that you have a value `rating` which can take integer values from 1 to 5. Each star will be an `img` element which can be filled or empty based on the rating.

```jsx
import React from 'react';
import PropTypes from 'prop-types';
import filledStar from './filledStar.png';
import emptyStar from './emptyStar.png';

class StarRating extends React.Component {
  render() {
    const stars = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
      if (i < this.props.rating) {
        stars.push(<img key={i} src={filledStar} alt="filled star"/>)
      } else {
        stars.push(<img key={i} src={emptyStar} alt="empty star"/>)
      }
    }

    return (
	  <div className='star-rating'>
	    {stars}
	  </div>
	);
  }
}

StarRating.propTypes = {
  rating: PropTypes.number.isRequired
};

export default StarRating;
```

Just replace `filledStar.png` and `emptyStar.png` with your actual star images. Also, you may want to add some CSS to style the stars as per your wish.

