    for character in input_string.lower():
        if character not in punctuation and character != ' ':
            word += character
        else:
            if word != "":
                words.append(word)
            word = ""
    if word != "":
        words.append(word)
    return words
```

Please note that it's better to use the built-in methods, like lower(), split(), translate(), etc., and the modules like string and re, for such operations as they are more readable, efficient and reduce the chance of error. In real-world programming, using such low-level solutions is not recommended.

